<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
  CGM Bolus Advisor

  A WORKED DESIGN OVER REAL CGM DATA (Don, 2026-09-11). One model holds a
  sensor reading and the therapy settings it is read against; one algorithm
  turns them into a correction dose, a carbohydrate dose and a trend
  adjustment, and refuses to dose at all below the low threshold.

  EVERY NUMBER IS MEASURED, which is the whole point of putting this on the
  AI Designer rather than in a spreadsheet: mg/dL cannot be compared with
  grams, and the design says so in the file.

  NOT MEDICAL ADVICE. It is a worked example of the arithmetic every pump and
  every bolus calculator does; the numbers in the data node are made up.
-->
<gorp name="CGM Bolus Advisor">
  <!-- nos-uml-state {"mode":"ai-design","title":"CGM Bolus Advisor","layout":{"cgm.bolus.Session":{"x":60,"y":60,"w":340,"h":320},"cgm.bolus.Morning":{"x":60,"y":430,"w":340,"h":320},"cgm.bolus.Advise":{"x":500,"y":140,"w":320,"h":200},"cgm.bolus.Dose":{"x":920,"y":140,"w":320,"h":240}}} -->

  <comment view="class">Everything the arithmetic needs, in one model, because SAI allows one model on an algorithm's port.

Session holds the CGM reading — glucose in mg/dL and the trend in mg/dL per minute, which is what a continuous monitor gives you that a finger stick does not — beside the therapy settings it has to be read against: target, low threshold, insulin sensitivity, carbohydrate ratio, insulin already on board and a maximum dose.

Morning is a data instance of Session with one plausible breakfast in it. Advise reads Session and writes Dose.

Two measurements worth looking at. The trend is \milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}\minute\tothe{-1} — a rate written with negative exponents rather than \per, so it grades Platinum and still reads as mg/dL/min on the chip. And an insulin unit has no SI dimension at all, so every dose row is declared \one: sensitivity is "mg/dL per unit", and per a dimensionless count that is just mg/dL.</comment>
  <expect>Check finds nothing — 0 errors, 0 warnings — so Run is available, and Run comes back OK. (xmlIT reads the body and discards it, so no dose comes back: this design says what to compute, it does not compute it here.)

The arithmetic it describes:
  correction = (glucose − target) / sensitivity
  carbDose   = carbs / carbRatio
  trendAdjust= trend × 30 min / sensitivity
  units      = max(0, correction + carbDose + trendAdjust − activeInsulin), capped at maxDose

Below the low threshold it must not dose at all: step 0 jumps straight to hold.

Two things this design is deliberately honest about. A glucose reading wants "keep the latest", and the server's collapse table allows Latest only on a date, so every reading here collapses Monotone instead — worth raising with Nick. And validate rules only compare rows of the same quantity: low against target in mg/dL, activeInsulin against maxDose in units. Compare glucose against carbs and Check must refuse it.</expect>

  <model namespace="cgm.bolus.Session">
    <variables>
      <variable name="id"       type="key" />
      <variable name="taken"    type="utcdatetime" collapse="Latest" />
      <variable name="glucose"  type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="trend"    type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}\minute\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="target"   type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="low"      type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/>
        <validate>low &lt; target</validate>
      </variable>
      <variable name="sensitivity"   type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="carbRatio"     type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\gram" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="carbs"         type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\gram" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="activeInsulin" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="maxDose"       type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/>
        <validate>activeInsulin &lt; maxDose</validate>
      </variable>
    </variables>
  </model>

  <data namespace="cgm.bolus.Morning" of="cgm.bolus.Session">
    <variables>
      <variable name="id"      type="key">CGM-DEMO</variable>
      <variable name="taken"   type="utcdatetime" collapse="Latest">2026-09-11T08:15:00Z</variable>
      <variable name="glucose" type="double" collapse="Monotone">196<unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="trend"   type="double" collapse="Monotone">1.4<unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}\minute\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="target"  type="double" collapse="Monotone">110<unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="low"     type="double" collapse="Monotone">70<unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="sensitivity"   type="double" collapse="Monotone">45<unit basis="\milli\gram\deci\litre\tothe{-1}" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="carbRatio"     type="double" collapse="Monotone">10<unit basis="\gram" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="carbs"         type="double" collapse="Monotone">45<unit basis="\gram" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="activeInsulin" type="double" collapse="Monotone">1.2<unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="maxDose"       type="double" collapse="Monotone">12<unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
    </variables>
  </data>

  <algorithm namespace="cgm.bolus.Advise">
    <input  model="cgm.bolus.Session" />
    <output model="cgm.bolus.Dose" />
    <operations>
      <operation name="correction"  returns="double" />
      <operation name="carbDose"    returns="double" />
      <operation name="trendAdjust" returns="double" />
      <operation name="advise"      returns="double" />
    </operations>
    <function>
      <expressions>
        <expression sequence="0" name="below the low threshold?">
          <If input="cgm.bolus.Session">
            <parameters>
              <parameter position="0">
                <Less input="cgm.bolus.Session" output="cgm.bolus.Dose.hold">
                  <parameters>
                    <parameter position="0"><pathvariable type="double" namespace="cgm.bolus.Session.glucose"/></parameter>
                    <parameter position="1"><pathvariable type="double" namespace="cgm.bolus.Session.low"/></parameter>
                  </parameters>
                </Less>
              </parameter>
              <parameter position="1"><goto sequence="4"/></parameter>
            </parameters>
          </If>
        </expression>
        <expression sequence="1" name="correction — the gap over the sensitivity" />
        <expression sequence="2" name="carbohydrate — the meal over the ratio" />
        <expression sequence="3" name="subtract insulin on board, floor at zero, cap at the maximum" />
        <expression sequence="4" name="hold — treat the low instead of dosing" />
      </expressions>
    </function>
  </algorithm>

  <model namespace="cgm.bolus.Dose">
    <variables>
      <variable name="correction"  type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="carbDose"    type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="trendAdjust" type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="units"       type="double" collapse="Monotone"><unit basis="\one" namespace="D-SI"/></variable>
      <variable name="hold"        type="bool" />
      <variable name="advice"      type="string" />
    </variables>
  </model>
</gorp>
